WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:10.470 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  this may look like a space mission  control center but it's actually a major  european fruit and vegetable auction in  belgium  it is run by bell orta one of the  largest fruit and veg selling  cooperatives in europe  every day up to four thousand tons of  fresh produce are sold here the  organization has strict produce  procedures to ensure good quality  standards and prices  for growers sustainable production also  means a fair income  we aim for the best possible price in  the markets  for the production of our growers we  also want to let the consumer enjoy our  fresh produce in a healthy way  if you want to build trust of the  consumer of even our buyers  and the production of our growers then  you're also looking at long-term  relationship between what happens on the  field what happens at the producer side  and what happens  at the consumer's home  fair market conditions sustainable  farming and quality standards are some  of the pillars of the eu's new common  agricultural policy cap its future goals  are to combine social economic and  environmental approaches to create a  sustainable model of european  agriculture  let's leave the auction and head to two  farms in puta and hala that are part of  the burlotta network  both farms have made changes to make  their production more sustainable thanks  to financial support from the cap  under this huge greenhouse where  thousands of tomato plants grow nothing  goes to waste  a cogeneration system produces  complementary energy which is released  into the local grid  thermal insulation screens help save  heat at night natural methods are used  to protect plants from disease and the  irrigation system ensures the most  efficient use of water  the water  the excess water is collected and after  it's purified  it is reused on the plants  so it's a closed cycle nothing goes to  waste  we also use the maximum amount of rain  in order to meet our water requirements  as efficiently as possible  also efficient  a led lighting system installed in the  greenhouse helps compensate the lack of  light during winter months  the advantage of led lights is that they  consume less power so we save energy  and we can also provide optimal light  for the plants needed  farms of all sizes are playing an  important role in the transition towards  a more eco-friendly agriculture  sustainable solutions like those used in  putter's tomato production are also used  in this family-owned strawberry farm in  hala  [Music]  they apply natural remedies to protect  plants from disease as well as using new  technology like this autonomous robot  that uses uv light to fight powdery  mildew it's a machine that helps reduce  the use of pesticides  we mainly use a natural strategy  we use organic and natural methods as  much as we can to fight plant diseases  only as a last option do we use  chemicals  of course it is important that we all  make these efforts because in the end it  does affect our final product there is  also a growing demand from consumers for  more environmentally friendly and  pesticide free fruits  [Music]

